Found by k260. `_prompt_hetzner_control_plane` prints `[!!] Could not read the Hetzner catalogue — keeping the defaults` and drops the exception, so a 401 (bad token), a 429 or a network failure gets no diagnosis on STDERR (house rule: an error line carries its diagnosis).

Done when the line names the cause (status/message from WWW::Hetzner, one line, no token in it), init still never fails over it, and a test pins a 401 and a network error. Lane: ocp-apply-worker.

